<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rembrandt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1669">1669</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Rembrandt van Rijn, Rembrandt Harmenszoon van Rijn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rembrandt van Rijn was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> painter, draughtsman and etcher, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiden">Leiden</a>, who worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> from the early 1630s. He is known for portraits, biblical scenes and a long series of self-portraits, and for his use of light and shadow, as in The Night Watch of 1642. Despite early success he went bankrupt in 1656, and he is regarded as the leading artist of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-golden-age">Dutch Golden Age</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rembrandt.jpg" alt="Rembrandt" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rembrandt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rembrandt_van_Rijn_-_Self-Portrait_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
